  "paper_scope": "The paper reports the first experimental realization of the unitary almost-Mathieu operator (UAMO) and its non-Hermitian extension (PUAMO) using single-photon quantum walks. It observes metal-insulator transitions in the Hermitian limit, PT-symmetry-breaking transitions, and a novel spectral transition where all quasienergies become purely imaginary. The selected quantitative cluster focuses on the Lyapunov exponent L_lambda1_lambda2_eta, which quantifies the inverse localization length and is given by L = max(0, log(lambda_0) - 2*pi*|eta|) with lambda_0 = lambda_2*(1+lambda_1')/(lambda_1*(1+lambda_2')). Two claims are built for the private regimes eta=0 and eta=0.1, sharing public controls lambda_1 and lambda_2 in [0.2,0.67] and the common readout lyapunov_exponent.",
