    {
      "mechanism_id": "lambda0_structure",
      "statement": "The Lyapunov exponent of the PUAMO is given by L = max(0, log(lambda_0) - 2*pi*|eta|), where lambda_0 = lambda_2*(1+lambda_1')/(lambda_1*(1+lambda_2')) with lambda_1' = sqrt(1-lambda_1^2) and lambda_2' = sqrt(1-lambda_2^2). This mechanism defines the structural constants used in the Lyapunov claims.",
